<!--Post: 1784--><!--Time: 1102856073-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1784"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 4:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is it possible that BTK worked at:  <BR> <BR>Olan Mills Portrait Studio  <BR>&#40;316&#41; 652-9952 8600 E Kellogg Dr  <BR>Wichita, KS  <BR> <BR>This studio is located right next to all the crimescenes, and not far from WSU and the libarary either.  <BR> <BR>Look at the piture of Vicky Wegerle on the frontpage of this forum,. Klick on the &#34;Offer To BTK&#34; and then klick on her name and a big version of the picture will appeare. In the lower left corner of the pic it says Olan Mills.  <BR> <BR>I think that this photo studio is the thing all the victims has in common.  <BR>I think it is possible that BTK worked there and choose his victims among the customers. He might have worked there at night and attended classes at WSU daytime.  <BR> <BR>Think about how big a part taking pictures was for BTK.  <BR> <BR>There was an insident including a photo, before Shirley Vian was killed .  <BR>&#34;The incident occurred during the daytime and there was no sign of forced entry. The killer had stopped one of the victim&#39;s sons on the street that morning, and showed him photographs of a woman and child, purportedly seeking directions to their home.&#34;  <BR> <BR>I think he had brought a copy of a picture of Shirly and one of her sons, that Shirly had have taken at the Olan Mills Portrait Studio...  <BR> <BR>Maaybe that was why he was let in without problems?, because he at the door said that he was from Olan Mills Portrait Studio, and they knew that they had their photo taken there?  <BR> <BR>I wonder if Olan Mills Portrait Studio was located at the same adress in the 70th and 80th?  <BR> <BR>Maybe somone on this board, who is located in Wichita , could call the studio and ask?  <BR>Here is the number:  <BR> <BR>Olan Mills Portrait Studio  <BR>&#40;316&#41; 652-9952 8600 E Kellogg Dr  <BR>Wichita, KS  <BR> <BR>I sure would like to know who worked at that studio in the 70th and 80th!  <BR> <BR>Anyone have more ideas or details from the killings that could support this theorie?  <BR> <BR>hugs...skov  <BR> <BR>  <BR>   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1784-->
<!--Post: 1800--><!--Time: 1102886625-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1800"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 1:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve been interested in the Olan Mills angle since I received the picture of Vicki a few months ago. <BR> <BR>This is a perfect example of why I feel it&#39;s so important to publish all of the materials I&#39;m able to collect; you never know where it may lead.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1800-->
<!--Post: 1805--><!--Time: 1102890850-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1805"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 12, 2004 - 2:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->exactly... that is the one thing that has been sticking out at me more than anything else in this whole thing....the picture and the fact that the killer had it BEFORE the crime... <BR>see this post:<a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/6/194.html?1102852010" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/6/194.html ?1102852010</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1805-->
<!--Post: 1823--><!--Time: 1102938037-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1823"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Truckinup<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Truckinup<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 13, 2004 - 3:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree, he has the hobby of taking pictures. Don&#39;t you think he would have to go to a camera supply store? <BR> <BR>Moler&#39;s Camera on Douglas is a small yet very precise place. I would also look there, if it was there in the 70&#39;s and 80&#39;s. I am pretty sure it was.  <BR>There is a few others, one is on Broadway as well. Broadway and Lincoln I am almost sure of. I don&#39;t have any means of checking it out. I will ASAP. <BR> <BR>Do you think that &#34;HE&#34; had the picture all along? That it was given to him by her? <BR>I think she knew him or talked to him a time or two, prior to her murder.  <BR> <BR>He mentioned his hobby as a ham radio operator. Anymore, you have to be registered and licensed in order to operate.  <BR> <BR>Just a few questions.. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1823-->
<!--Post: 1850--><!--Time: 1103023295-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1850"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brazilian<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brazilian<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 3:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey there, everybody! First time poster. <BR> <BR>I think BTK is strongly connected with photography and might be connected with Olan Mills Studio as well. <BR>All this stuff about drawings, sketches, leave the body on a certain position sounds to me as somebody crazy about portraits, photographs, modelling, etc. <BR> <BR>I also think Tom might think this way. Maybe that´s why he keeps putting those portraits on the top of the news page. <BR> <BR>Tom, can you tell us if Nancy Fox´s portrait was taken at Olan Mills? <BR> <BR>Maybe BTK worked there, had access to the customer portraits or used to hang around there to choose his victims. <BR> <BR>Also, and this have already been said, I think his manner of speak, like &#34;That is correct&#34; or &#34;Homicide, Nancy Fox&#34; shows that he has some intimacy with radio-operator-talking as he knows to communicate briefly and clearly. <BR> <BR>I think that all these Olan Mills information and theories are very important. <BR> <BR>Sorry about any english mistakes!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1850-->
<!--Post: 2019--><!--Time: 1103251340-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2019"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Faithful_reader<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Faithful_reader<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 6:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I hate to be a wet blanket on the Olan Mills thing but I don&#39;t think it&#39;s terribly significant that more than one victim had portraits done at Olan Mills.  During that time, EVERYONE  had their portraits done by Olan Mills.  They were slightly more upscale than the Wal-Mart type studios that are everywhere now, but certainly affordable to average income families.  I would guess that at least half the houses on any street during that time would have a portrait with the distinctive gold printing in the corner.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2019-->
<!--Post: 2164--><!--Time: 1103344032-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2164"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 8:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another thought on the Olan mills idea...Those studios back then didnt do their own processing. That sent out to a &#39;package printer&#39; a pro-lab that would do it for them...He couldve worked there and had access to all the pics taken at any of the local studios...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2164-->
<!--Post: 2207--><!--Time: 1103414167-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2207"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Josef_carlin<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Josef_carlin<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 18, 2004 - 3:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yet another thought. BTK was described as carrying a  bag with him to his crimes. Some described it as a &#34;doctors bag.&#34; While most formal portraits are taken in a studio, it is not unknown for less formal portraits to be taken in the home. Photographer would carry cameras, lenses, film, and other accessories in a camera bag. You also might want to look a my post on this board under Letters titled &#34;The Killman Letter Anagram&#34; for another possible Olan Mills connection.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2207-->
<!--Post: 2208--><!--Time: 1103414633-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2208"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 18, 2004 - 4:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lets assume for a minute that the pics he took at the scenes WEREN&#39;T poloroids then he musta had a home dark room set up...not too difficult to do. Anyone with a high school background in photography could set up a black and white darkroom...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2208-->
<!--Post: 2209--><!--Time: 1103414862-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2209"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 18, 2004 - 4:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another thought. Its interesting that TRAINS,HAM RADIO, and PHOTOGRAPHY are somewhat related. Most of my ham friends are also into the other 2 interests...not sure why we all tend to do these 3 things...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2209-->
<!--Post: 2285--><!--Time: 1103497464-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2285"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:hackenmaster@cox.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Wichitan<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wichitan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 19, 2004 - 3:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just a side note, there was an olan mills location, located at central and west street, and this was close to some of the murder scenes as well.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2285-->
<!--Post: 5804--><!--Time: 1107387317-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5804"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lmuncy316<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lmuncy316<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 3:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->When I graduated from high school I missed my senior photo session taken at school.  So, I went to the local Olan Mills and had my picture taken.  My cousin did the same thing the following year.  I found out that Olan Mills did all of the pictures for our senior class and yearbook pictures.  Maybe Olan Mills did the same thing for the University in Wichita.  Which, would connect BTK to Olan Mills and the copier at the University.  However, as important as I believe it would be to connect BTK to the copier and Olin Mills, I believe it would be easier to focus on the victims connections to these places.  After all, we know more about the victims than we do BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5804-->
